[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5144052529","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120421#issuecomment-5144052529","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120421","id":5144052529,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMpwDMQ","user":{"login":"DragonFerocity","id":13317384,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMzE3Mzg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13317384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DragonFerocity","html_url":"https://github.com/DragonFerocity","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DragonFerocity/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DragonFerocity/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DragonFerocity/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DragonFerocity/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DragonFerocity/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DragonFerocity/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DragonFerocity/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DragonFerocity/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DragonFerocity/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-31T14:37:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T14:40:54Z","body":"I am also having this issue in my project, though my setup is different\n\nSubViewportContainer\n|- Control Nodes\nMeshInstance3D\n\nThe mesh instance is a plane mesh with a StandardMaterial3D with a ViewportTexture set as the Albedo\n\nNote: When running the game from Godot, the textures show up correctly. This is isolated to the editor for me. I can also fix it by closing and re-opening the scene. It's only if the scene is loaded upon Godot's initial load or re-load","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5144052529/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5163453182","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120421#issuecomment-5163453182","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120421","id":5163453182,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM8QK_g","user":{"login":"include-xb","id":121707744,"node_id":"U_kgDOB0Ec4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121707744?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb","html_url":"https://github.com/include-xb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-03T07:21:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-03T07:22:44Z","body":"( Come from a student in China )\n\nI encountered the same issue in my project. \n\n### Version\nGodot v4.7.stable.official [5b4e0cb0f]\n\n### System Infomation\n- Windows 11\n- Vulkan (Forward+)\n- NIVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 LapTop GPU 596.13\n\n### Detail\nWhen I open my project, the TextureRect is: \n\n<img width=\"2560\" height=\"1528\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fc1b3e92-1b48-4c99-9856-685b52471b6f\" />\n\nThen I clear the Texture of TextureRect: \n\n<img width=\"2560\" height=\"1528\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c9269b09-4e67-4928-b14a-83ba970e77db\" />\n\nReload the expected ViewportTexture:\n\n<img width=\"529\" height=\"1097\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d609457-cbfd-4916-bb62-5a1cfd1800c5\" />\n\nChoose the expected SubViewport: \n\n<img width=\"885\" height=\"362\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e5786bdb-1dea-4aad-ac94-0e76b22a0e26\" />\n\nNow the ViewportTexture is loaded correctly:\n\n<img width=\"2560\" height=\"1528\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4510617f-594a-4635-8d8e-82262dc97824\" />\n\nHowever, when I start running the project, the Viewport can be rendered correctly. As @DragonFerocity said: \n\n> It's only if the scene is loaded upon Godot's initial load or re-load\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5163453182/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5468515480","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120421#issuecomment-5468515480","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120421","id":5468515480,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRfLsmA","user":{"login":"include-xb","id":121707744,"node_id":"U_kgDOB0Ec4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121707744?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb","html_url":"https://github.com/include-xb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/include-xb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-30T11:52:17Z","updated_at":"2026-08-30T11:52:17Z","body":"@AThousandShips @DragonFerocity @thorwin99 \nIt seems that I found the solution to this issue.\nToday I tried to export my project. When the `.exe` file was created, Godot gave me an error message: invalid path to SubViewport. \nThen I changed the parent node of SubViewport so that it is **the child node of the `TextureRect`.** After that, no error message was shown. Additionally, the `TextureRect` with the `ViewportTexture` rendered correctly. \n\n**The most important thing is:** if you want to add a `ViewportTexture` to a node, you should set the `SubViewport` node as **the child of** that node.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5468515480/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]